course: dictionary
lesson: 11930
title: Short words and what they stand for
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some long words get shortened so they are quicker to say. Camo is short for camouflage. Context helps you work out the meaning: «He wore camo trousers and a green cap to the woods.» Green and woods are clues that camo has something to do with colours that match nature.
explain: Camo can be a noun or an adjective. As a noun it means the pattern itself, or clothes with that pattern: «He bought new camo for his trip.» As an adjective it describes things: «The camo jacket helped him hide among the trees.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If camouflage fits, you have found the right meaning. Camo is informal, so it is fine to use with friends, but use camouflage in formal writing.
fact: Camo is short for camouflage.
fact: Camouflage means colours or patterns that help something blend into its background.
fact: Camo trousers and caps, in greens and browns, are popular fashion.
fact: In science, chameleons use camouflage to hide from enemies.
fact: In video games, players can unlock camo skins to change how their character looks.
exercise: «He wore camo trousers and a green cap to the woods.» What does camo mean here? | Loud, bright, and easy to spot | *Clothes with a pattern that helps you blend in | A sort of tree | A kind of cake
exercise: Camo is short for which longer word? | *camouflage | cameo | campsite | comedy
exercise: «In the game, Sam unlocked a gold camo skin.» Where might you find camo skins? | On a train timetable | In a school library | In a cookery book | *In a video game
test: Which word is camo a short form of? | cameo | campfire | *camouflage | camera
test: Which sentence uses camo as an adjective? | Camo is short for camouflage. | She sat in the camo. | *The camo cap hid his hair. | He bought some camo for the trip.
exam: Which word could replace camo in «He wore camo to hide in the forest»? | chocolate | castle | cuddle | *camouflage
